       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day for extended-release. The usual maximum single dose is 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The order is about twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
